            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Franklin's Public Service</strong><br>\nBeyond his scientific achievements, Franklin was also a public servant. He helped establish the first public lending library in America and the first volunteer fire department in Philadelphia. He was involved in politics, serving as an agent representing Pennsylvania and other colonies in England. Franklin argued against the Stamp Act, helping to repeal it.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Benjamin Franklin's Role in the American Revolution</strong><br>\nWhen relations between the American colonies and Great Britain deteriorated, Franklin became an ardent supporter of American independence. He was part of the Second Continental Congress and helped to draft the Declaration of Independence. He was also a diplomat, securing crucial military and financial support from France during the Revolutionary War.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Postwar Achievements and Constitution</strong><br>\nAfter the war, Franklin continued to serve as a diplomat, signing the Treaty of Paris which ended the Revolutionary War. He returned to the United States in 1785 and became President of the Executive Council of Pennsylvania. He was a delegate to the Constitutional Convention in 1787, where he played a significant role in shaping the new American government.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
